<title>USA: Brazil coffee expects continued fair weather - WSC.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee expects continued fair weather - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The upper level ridge of high pressure aloft over Brazil's coffee belt is expected to remain in place through the beginning of next week, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A weak high pressure system is forecast to build out of Argentina over the weekend, but the high pressure system in place should prevent the new system from moving into the coffee belt, according to WSC.</p>
<p>Mostly fair weather was reported in the region overnight. Temperatures remained near to above normal with lows in the 50's and low 60's F (12-16 C).</p>
<p>Continued fair skies are expected through Thursday with the slight chance of showers developing in northern areas of the belt. Temperatures should average near to above normal for the week. The lowest temperatures through Sunday will remain above 50 F (10 C)</p>
<p>&quot;There is no frost or freeze in sight,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
